% ── decide ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% ⚑ A DECISION ITEM IS CLOSED WHILE DECIDED — it is not debt.  Its witness
% discriminates on whether the decision is LEGIBLE (recorded where a reader will
% find it), never on whether it was the right call.  There is deliberately no
% always-true `premise:` verb here: paperkit's own Δ grader marks a check that
% cannot fail `indeterminate`, and an unfalsifiable claim the gate certifies is
% worse than no claim at all.
